The smallest four-digit number is 1000. We'll start by identifying the Pascal's triangle rows where the entries are four-digit numbers. The first few rows are so small that the entries are not four-digit numbers. We'll iterate through the rows to find the smallest four-digit number and then find the second smallest one.

